Description: Windows 7, 8 and 10 style Task Manager with a Linux "Tux mode"
 Shows running applications, processes, services, startup programs, users
 and live CPU, memory, disk, network and GPU graphs, laid out like the Task
 Manager of Windows 7, Windows 8 or Windows 10.
 .
 Tux mode keeps the chosen layout and adds what only Linux reports: kernel
 process states, systemd units, cgroups, OOM scores, USS/PSS memory,
 pressure stall information, sensors and CPU vulnerabilities.
